Subject: WPE on Phoenix: the UI process lets the web process render one frame ahead (opt-in)

AcceleratedBackingStore sends FrameDone to the web process when WPEView's buffer-rendered fires,
i.e. when the compositor's wl_surface.frame callback for that frame comes, and the web process's
ThreadedCompositor does not composite again until FrameDone (State::InProgress until
frameComplete()). WPEViewWayland cannot have two frames in flight either (it RELEASE_ASSERTs on a
second render_buffer before the frame callback). So exactly one frame is in flight, and every
stage of the path runs in series once per frame: the web process's composite (with shared-memory
frames also its GPU readback into the ShareableBitmap), this process's copy of the frame into a
wl_shm pool, the compositor's upload of it, its composite and its wait for the next vblank. On the
Raspberry Pi 4 (labwc on the V3D, a 1000x620 view, CPU raster, shared-memory frames) that held a
30 fps <video> to ~10 composited frames per second whatever the video's size, and labwc flipped
once per composited frame: the sum of the stages, not any one of them, sets the rate.

With WPE_PHOENIX_FRAME_AHEAD=1 (wpe-browser --frame-ahead) FrameDone goes as soon as a frame has
been committed to the compositor, so the web process renders frame N+1 while the compositor shows
frame N. A frame that arrives while frame N still waits for its frame callback is held as the
pending buffer (the web process sends no further frame until its FrameDone, so at most one is
held) and committed from bufferRendered(); its FrameDone goes then. Still exactly one FrameDone
per Frame, still at most one frame committed per frame callback, so the web process runs at most
one frame ahead of the screen and requestAnimationFrame stays paced by the compositor. The web
process's swap chain holds the committed, the held and the rendering target (4 at most). The rate
becomes that of the slower side instead of the sum of both; latency grows by up to one frame.

Off by default until the Pi's A/B (wpe-browser's b8.sh transport). The UI process says which
pacing a view uses, once per backing store:

  WPEB-WEBKIT frame-pacing pid=<p> ahead=0|1

diff --git a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/wpe/AcceleratedBackingStore.h b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/wpe/AcceleratedBackingStore.h
--- a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/wpe/AcceleratedBackingStore.h
+++ b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/wpe/AcceleratedBackingStore.h
@@ -110,6 +110,14 @@
     HashMap<uint64_t, GRefPtr<WPEBuffer>> m_buffers;
     HashMap<WPEBuffer*, uint64_t> m_bufferIDs;
     std::optional<unsigned> m_targetBufferCount;
+#if OS(PHOENIX)
+    // One frame ahead (WPE_PHOENIX_FRAME_AHEAD=1): FrameDone goes when a frame is committed to the
+    // compositor, not when its frame callback comes; a frame that arrives while the previous one
+    // still waits for its callback is held in m_pendingBuffer until then.
+    bool m_frameAhead { false };
+    bool m_waitingForFrameCallback { false };
+    bool m_isRenderingBuffer { false };
+#endif
 };
 
 } // namespace WebKit
diff --git a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/wpe/AcceleratedBackingStore.cpp b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/wpe/AcceleratedBackingStore.cpp
--- a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/wpe/AcceleratedBackingStore.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/wpe/AcceleratedBackingStore.cpp
@@ -37,6 +37,13 @@
 #include <wtf/TZoneMallocInlines.h>
 #include <wtf/glib/GUniquePtr.h>
 
+#if OS(PHOENIX)
+#include <stdlib.h>
+#include <string.h>
+#include <unistd.h>
+#include <wtf/SetForScope.h>
+#endif
+
 #if OS(ANDROID)
 #include <drm/drm_fourcc.h>
 #elif USE(LIBDRM)
@@ -85,6 +92,18 @@
         auto& backingStore = *static_cast<AcceleratedBackingStore*>(userData);
         backingStore.toplevelChanged();
     }), this);
+
+#if OS(PHOENIX)
+    // Phoenix-RTOS: with one frame in flight, the web process composites frame N+1 only after the
+    // compositor's frame callback for frame N, so every cost of the path adds up per frame: the
+    // web process's composite (and, with shared-memory frames, its GPU readback), this process's
+    // copy into wl_shm, the compositor's upload and its wait for the next vblank. One frame ahead,
+    // the web process renders the next frame while the compositor shows this one, so the frame
+    // rate is set by the slower side instead of their sum (wpe-browser --frame-ahead).
+    const char* frameAhead = getenv("WPE_PHOENIX_FRAME_AHEAD");
+    m_frameAhead = frameAhead && !strcmp(frameAhead, "1");
+    WTFLogAlways("WPEB-WEBKIT frame-pacing pid=%d ahead=%d", getpid(), m_frameAhead);
+#endif
 }
 
 AcceleratedBackingStore::~AcceleratedBackingStore()
@@ -286,6 +305,15 @@
     if (!wpe_view_get_toplevel(m_wpeView.get()))
         return;
 
+#if OS(PHOENIX)
+    // One frame ahead: the frame on its way to the screen has not had its frame callback yet, so
+    // this one waits here; bufferRendered() commits it.
+    if (m_frameAhead && m_waitingForFrameCallback)
+        return;
+    SetForScope isRenderingBuffer(m_isRenderingBuffer, true);
+    m_waitingForFrameCallback = true;
+#endif
+
     // Rely on the layout of IntRect matching that of WPERectangle
     // to pass directly a pointer below instead of using copies.
     static_assert(sizeof(WebCore::IntRect) == sizeof(WPERectangle));
@@ -296,10 +324,19 @@
     GUniqueOutPtr<GError> error;
     if (!wpe_view_render_buffer(m_wpeView.get(), m_pendingBuffer.get(), rects, m_pendingDamageRects.size(), &error.outPtr())) {
         g_warning("Failed to render frame: %s", error->message);
+#if OS(PHOENIX)
+        m_waitingForFrameCallback = false;
+#endif
         frameDone();
         m_pendingBuffer = nullptr;
-    } else
+    } else {
         m_committedBuffer = WTF::move(m_pendingBuffer);
+#if OS(PHOENIX)
+        // The web process may render the next frame now, while the compositor shows this one.
+        if (m_frameAhead)
+            frameDone();
+#endif
+    }
     m_pendingDamageRects = { };
 }
 
@@ -311,6 +348,17 @@
 
 void AcceleratedBackingStore::bufferRendered()
 {
+#if OS(PHOENIX)
+    m_waitingForFrameCallback = false;
+    if (m_frameAhead) {
+        // This frame's FrameDone went when it was committed. A frame held meanwhile goes to the
+        // compositor now, unless its rendering fence is still pending (the fence monitor commits
+        // it then) or this is the view answering synchronously from inside renderPendingBuffer().
+        if (!m_isRenderingBuffer && m_webPage && m_pendingBuffer && !m_fenceMonitor.hasFileDescriptor())
+            renderPendingBuffer();
+        return;
+    }
+#endif
     frameDone();
 }
 
